"Let $P_{t,k}=P_3|P_k$ be the graph with $k+1$ vertices obtained by gluing a triangle and a $k$-gon along an edge. Let $w^1_{{\\mathcal A}_3}(G)$ be the width of the torsion in $H^{1,*}_{{\\mathcal A}_3}(G)$, namely the maximal torsion grading minus the minimal torsion grading, with value $-1$ when all cohomology is free. **Width conjecture for $P_{t,k}$.** For these graphs,\n\n$$\nw^1_{{\\mathcal A}_3}(P_{t,k})=k-3.\n$$\n\nThe formula is based on the displayed computations for this family; the source does not state a resolution."